        "kind": "paper",
        "label": "Nov 16, 2026 10:20 AM CT",
        "note": "Recently an artificial intelligence proved an 18-year-old conjecture in computer science, called the Aaronson–Ambainis conjecture. The proof settles a long-standing conjecture (educated guess) that eliminates one proposed route to enormous quantum computer speedups, ruling out one particular variant of \"quantum supremacy,\" the term for the hypothesis that a programmable quantum computer can solve a problem that no classical computer can solve in any \"feasible\" amount of time.",
